{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/x8vmlo36","slide":5,"text":"05","textPreview":"05","textChars":2,"textLines":1,"bbox":[1165,682,72,22]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/tu0ld2","slide":5,"text":"Form teams of three or four and assign one recorder. Read the task exactly once, then ask teams to restate the acceptance condition in their own words. During work time, circulate and ask evidence questions rather than supplying answers. At the critique, require another team to identify one strength, one contract gap, and one unsafe assumption. Give teams five minutes to repair the artifact before debrief. Collect the final artifact as course evidence; it will become input to the capstone. If time compresses, protect the critique and repair steps—the learning comes from validation, not only drafting.\n\n[Sources]\n- Code Review Harness repository: contracts/style-and-validation.md; contracts/sandboxed-contract-evolution.md; governance/integration-boundaries.md"}
